# qingshan-skills Cursor adapter

Apply this adapter before responding to or acting on any software engineering
request. It loads the canonical methodology instead of duplicating runtime-
specific workflow summaries.

## Resolve the skills root

Never assume the current workspace root is the qingshan-skills repository.

Choose the first path that is a full qingshan-skills root. A full root must
contain all of: `SKILL.md`, `ETHOS.md`, and
`skills/{clarify,plan,execute,investigate,verify,reflect}/SKILL.md`.

1. Environment variable `QINGSHAN_SKILLS_ROOT`, if set and complete
2. Absolute path baked by `scripts/install-cursor-project-rule.sh` as
   `QINGSHAN_SKILLS_ROOT_BAKED` below (when present and complete)
3. `~/.qingshan-skills/repo` when that directory is a complete clone or worktree
4. The current workspace root only when it is a complete qingshan-skills root
   and the root `AGENTS.md` identifies the project as `qingshan-skills`

If a higher-priority candidate is set but incomplete, skip it and try the next
candidate instead of stopping early.

QINGSHAN_SKILLS_ROOT_BAKED=

If no candidate resolves, stop and report that qingshan-skills is not installed
for this Cursor project. Do not reconstruct the workflow from memory. Do not
read the consumer project's own root `SKILL.md` unless step 4 matched.

## Load order

1. Read `<skills-root>/SKILL.md` completely.
2. Read `<skills-root>/ETHOS.md` completely.
3. Use the root router to classify the request and select the lightest safe
   workflow under Risk Classification Floors.
4. Read `<skills-root>/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` completely before applying it.
5. Continue to use canonical files under `<skills-root>` when a workflow handoff
   changes the selected skill.

Respond in the user's current conversation language unless they explicitly ask
for another language.
